{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery","id":1165571,"title":"Homebrew: Arcane Archery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-06T07:52:40-08:00","id":1165571,"title":"Homebrew: Arcane Archery","content":"I had a lot of free time and tried to develop a new fighting style for mages based on archery and inspired by the Arcane Archer class in D&amp;D. I'm not certain it is a very good / useful / balanced / flavourful Merit so I would appreciate criticism. <hr /><br /> <b>Arcane Archery (Style, 1-5)</b><br /> Prerequisites: Adamantine Arrows Status 1, Firearms 2 (or 2 dots in whatever skill your group uses for archery), Wits OR Composure 3 and one Arcana with dots equal to or greater than dots in Arcane Archery.<br /> <br /> Humans have been using bows and arrows for many thousands of years and the symbolism of accuracy, precision and penetration is well ingrained into the fallen world. Slowly but surely some warlike mages have learned how to use and apply this symbolism and weave their spellcasting and archery together as one. This style is actually 10 different styles; the mage dedicates one Arcana to their Arcane Archery and will have different benefits depending on what Arcana they chose.<br /> <br /> At the Storyteller's discretion this style can be applied to modern firearms as well. While this is a style exclusive for archers and based on the thousands of years of archery traditions, firearms have been around for a few hundred years so it is not unreasonable that progressive mages have worked this style into these weapons instead.<br /> <br /> 1 - Zen Archery<br /> Using bows and arrows as strong symbolism for truth, accuracy and precision the mage can use their magic to massively enhance their mundane vigilance, gaining a bonus to mundane perception equal to their Arcane Archery dots.<br /> <br /> 2 - Imbued arrows<br /> The mage has learned how to allow spells to travel with the arrows they fire. If they spend 1 mana and take a turn to cast a spell on an arrow that arrow can then deliver the spell to where it is fired. Thus, the mage avoids spending Reach to make a spell Sensory. This of course requires a successful shooting roll and the spell will dissipate if it is not discharged during its duration. This can only be done with spells from the Arcanum the mage chose for this Merit, so a Death archer can only deliver Death spells this way.<br /> <br /> 3 - Archer's Eye<br /> The mage can spend 1 mana to reflexively use their magic to gain a one-shot boost to their natural archery skills. This can be done even after the dice are rolled. The bonus received depends on their dedicated Arcana:<br /> Death: Arrows travel partially through twilight, ignoring penalties due to concealment and cover equal to dots in Arcane Archery. The mage in this way can also deal damage to ghosts and other deathly ephemera in twilight. In addition, this damage is metaphysically strong and is considered Resistant.<br /> Fate: Using a bow and arrow the mage can get an Exceptional Success with 3 successes instead of 5.<br /> Forces: Forceful arrows causes the Knocked Down Tilt in addition to damage.<br /> Life: A combination of enhanced muscle-memory and perception eliminates penalties due to range and concealment equal to dots in Arcane Archery.<br /> Matter: Gain a bonus to armor piercing equal to dots in Arcane Archery.<br /> Mind: A successful hit pierces mind as well as flesh and bereaves the target of Willpower, up to the archer's dots in Arcane Archery.<br /> Prime: Ignore Mage Armor equal to dots in Arcane Archery.<br /> Space: Seeker arrows eliminate penalties due to range and concealment equal to dots in Arcane Archery.<br /> Spirit: Arrows travel partially through twilight, ignoring penalties due to concealment and cover equal to dots in Arcane Archery. The mage in this way can also deal damage to spirits and other deathly ephemera in twilight. Alternately, the mage can pierce the Gauntlet with her arrows to strike at spirits on the other side. Spirits targetted this way gains a bonus Defense equal to Gauntlet strength.<br /> Time: The mage automatically goes first in initiative this round. If another character has a similar ability the two characters compare initiative normally.<br /> <br /> 4 - Eldritch Arrows<br /> The mage never needs to carry ammunition again if they do not wish so. At the cost of 1 Mana the mage simply creates arrows automatically when they fire their bows for the duration of the scene, whether using ambient materials such as light (Forces), air particles (Matter) or microorganisms (Life), or even using the forces of chance (Fate), entropy (Death) or truth itself (Prime).<br /> <br /> 5 - Arrow of Unmaking<br /> If the mage pays 1 Mana their arrow is fused with Unmaking itself. If successfully hit by the arrow of the mage, the target must succeed on a Clash of Wills test against the Gnosis + Arcana of the character or die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 12-08-2017, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T09:43:00-08:00","id":1165600,"title":"","content":"Nice. A good blend.<br /> <br /> I feel like Spirit should be able to let you shoot across the Gauntlet (treated the Gauntlet Penalty as a Defense bonus for the target). Not sure what to do with Death to bring that up to parity. Mind <i>maybe</i> should also do the same for Goetia. Just throwing ideas out, but what about letting them bypass non-X targets? Such as Mind arrows going straight through unthinking matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T14:03:12-08:00","id":1165667,"title":"","content":"The fifth dot is quite scary. <br /> <br /> Thoughts on alternate effects for the third dot:<br /> Prime - can challenge magical auto-protections against missiles with a Clash of Wills<br /> Forces - inflicts the Knocked Down Tilt<br /> Fate - delivers a hex upon hit<br /> Time - ignored Defense like Firearms (if used with Firearms, ignores even Defense against Firearms)<br /> Mind - hits things in Mind-Twilight, depletes target\u2019s Willpower<br /> Space - ignores range &amp; concealment<br /> Spirit - hits things in Spirit-Twilight, depletes target\u2019s Essence<br /> Life - inflicts the Sick Tilt<br /> Death - hits things in Death-Twilight, damage dealt becomes resistant<br /> Matter - reduces Durability of hit objects, gain Armor Piercing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T18:13:54-08:00","id":1165722,"title":"","content":"Everything you have listed is just an ability that Mages can already posses, such as Imbued Arrow just being a form of Aimed Spell, so dressing them up in fluff and giving an enhancement to justify the cost of a merit seems balanced to me. I especially like the variations based on the character's Arcana, it helps make each Archer feel unique and would make very flavorful Mage traditions.<br /> \u200bOne question, would you require the character to rebuy the third and fourth dot for each Arcanum applied, or would one purchase allow the effect of all Arcanum available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T23:12:36-08:00","id":1166027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1165600#post1165600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. A good blend.<br /> <br /> I feel like Spirit should be able to let you shoot across the Gauntlet (treated the Gauntlet Penalty as a Defense bonus for the target). Not sure what to do with Death to bring that up to parity. Mind <i>maybe</i> should also do the same for Goetia. Just throwing ideas out, but what about letting them bypass non-X targets? Such as Mind arrows going straight through unthinking matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I will consider letting Spirit arrows cross straight through the Gauntlet, seems like an interesting ability when combatting spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T23:18:57-08:00","id":1166028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1165722#post1165722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything you have listed is just an ability that Mages can already posses, such as Imbued Arrow just being a form of Aimed Spell, so dressing them up in fluff and giving an enhancement to justify the cost of a merit seems balanced to me. I especially like the variations based on the character's Arcana, it helps make each Archer feel unique and would make very flavorful Mage traditions.<br /> \u200bOne question, would you require the character to rebuy the third and fourth dot for each Arcanum applied, or would one purchase allow the effect of all Arcanum available?</div> </div> </div> </div>About Imbued Arrow; it is designed to make the mage's Aimed Spells even more dangerous because you cannot apply Defense against arrows unlike Aimed Spells. I also forgot to specify that you can only do it with spells from the dedicated Arcanum, so a &quot;Death archer&quot; can only do it with Death spells. I will edit it shortly, when I have the time.<br /> <br /> I briefly thought about doing this as a Legacy but decided that it would be more flavourful and interesting to present different abilities for each Arcanum instead.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of having requiring the character to buy this merit separately for each Arcanum effect, because of the specific mudras and traditions associated with each archer school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 12-08-2017, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T15:36:47-08:00","id":1167432,"title":"","content":"Your second level (Imbued arrows) sounds more like it should be Prime's schtick to me than a general benefit, even so.<br /> <br /> Creating weapons from nothing is a pretty major ability. Fate ammunition should be a roll to see if you luck out and stumble across something appropriate. Spirit and Death should have penalties based on being intangible or immaterial with the concomitant advantage of having the substance quite available. Matter could have the drawback that coalescing or drawing an arrow takes a moment, but is just shy of always available. Mind could be fun: instead of physical damage, the arrows could be imbued with emotions or target Doors. That deserve some more thought. Space, well, I'm actually kinda thinking that establishing a Sensory bond to an arrow fired for a few moments rather than providing ammunition could work. Maybe allow conjuring arrows from wherever they happen to be, instead. Life could allow drawing of an arrow out of a tree, maybe. That would fit the flaw from Matter. Perhaps allow Life to disease or poison a target, though, perhaps even crippling them.<br /> <br /> Another take is that the merit allows spells of the arcana to be shot from a bow as if an arrow, without needing a real one. That's still quite useful.<br /> <br /> 5th is absurdly overpowered. I honestly don't mind an insta-kill very much for Death, (though that would be Making) given the arcana requirements you listed for the style, and the fluff fits Life, as well, but otherwise, it's pretty off-theme for the rest of the arcana. Spirit Bane, Ghost Eater, and things like that sound better. Of course, there really isn't any point to even <i>have</i> such a level in the merit. With the spread you already have listed, you just need to imbue an Unmaking (or Making Death) spell into the arrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T01:11:07-08:00","id":1167849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1167432#post1167432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your second level (Imbued arrows) sounds more like it should be Prime's schtick to me than a general benefit, even so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats may be true, and a good way to diversify a bit besides. I'll have to think about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creating weapons from nothing is a pretty major ability. Fate ammunition should be a roll to see if you luck out and stumble across something appropriate. Spirit and Death should have penalties based on being intangible or immaterial with the concomitant advantage of having the substance quite available. Matter could have the drawback that coalescing or drawing an arrow takes a moment, but is just shy of always available. Mind could be fun: instead of physical damage, the arrows could be imbued with emotions or target Doors. That deserve some more thought. Space, well, I'm actually kinda thinking that establishing a Sensory bond to an arrow fired for a few moments rather than providing ammunition could work. Maybe allow conjuring arrows from wherever they happen to be, instead. Life could allow drawing of an arrow out of a tree, maybe. That would fit the flaw from Matter. Perhaps allow Life to disease or poison a target, though, perhaps even crippling them. </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea is that by the time you have the fourth dot you also have at least 4 dots in your dedicated Arcana, so it is lika an extension of the Patterning practice. I do realize however that it is a hard sell for some of the Arcana. How about not having it cost a Mana to use but each Arcanum instead have one of those limitations you mention?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another take is that the merit allows spells of the arcana to be shot from a bow as if an arrow, without needing a real one. That's still quite useful. </div> </div> </div><br /> So make the second ability the fourth instead?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5th is absurdly overpowered. I honestly don't mind an insta-kill very much for Death, (though that would be Making) given the arcana requirements you listed for the style, and the fluff fits Life, as well, but otherwise, it's pretty off-theme for the rest of the arcana. Spirit Bane, Ghost Eater, and things like that sound better. Of course, there really isn't any point to even <i>have</i> such a level in the merit. With the spread you already have listed, you just need to imbue an Unmaking (or Making Death) spell into the arrow. </div> </div> </div>I know you could just attach an Unmaking spell to an arrow and slay that way. Doing it as a Merit though does not force you to make a Wisdom roll, since it is more like an Attainment rather than a spell and so does not count as an act of hubris. Is my line of thinking incorrect?<br /> <br /> I suppose I could just have the fifth dot replicate an adequate Unmaking (or Making) spell instead for each Arcanum where Death and Life of course would mean utter annihilation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T01:56:32-08:00","id":1168139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1167849#post1167849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is that by the time you have the fourth dot you also have at least 4 dots in your dedicated Arcana, so it is lika an extension of the Patterning practice. I do realize however that it is a hard sell for some of the Arcana. How about not having it cost a Mana to use but each Arcanum instead have one of those limitations you mention?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it <i>is</i> patterning, you need a distinct example of the arcana to manipulate in ways that fall under its purview, which is where those suggestions came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1167849#post1167849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So make the second ability the fourth instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. that sounds a bit better to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1167849#post1167849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you could just attach an Unmaking spell to an arrow and slay that way. Doing it as a Merit though does not force you to make a Wisdom roll, since it is more like an Attainment rather than a spell and so does not count as an act of hubris. Is my line of thinking incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments alter a soul to accept the attainment, which is why they don't cause a breaking point. Merits don't do that. This is essentially a fighting style, is it not? <br /> <br /> I do like making each arcanum very distinct because, well, they are supposed to be. That said, one thing you might consider is the final merit being some sort of swanky Yantra upgrade. Perhaps make arrows and archery-related yantras give bonus points or not count against totals or something.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, I'm thinking you really want these to be attainments in a legacy. That would get you the entire package. It would suggest narrowing down the arcana involved, which would also allow you to select the arcana to fit your vision more precisely. I'm seeing Death or Spirit, Prime, Matter, Fate or Space off the top o' my noggin. Most of my thinking is essentially what I said before. An archery familiar would be a great explanation for arrows at need. A guiding ancestor spirit could explain a few things via Death.<br /> <br /> Then again, there are odder options. I've been pondering how rules for &quot;Mystery Attainments&quot; would work, irrespective of this notion, but it could apply. I think a martial art that reveals mystery attainments about archery could be a really interesting story element, personally. Basically, the idea is having attainments that represent mysteries that need to be uncovered through grueling mystical questing, revealed by one who knows them, or researched by deconstructing rotes created by those who understood them. Apart from how they are obtained, they'd be arcana attainments. I expect these, or something akin, in the upcoming supplement, so I haven't spent too much grey time on the puzzle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T12:37:33-08:00","id":1169979,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> For the 4th power, why not explain it more as Pattern Restoration? The Bow and Arrows (or Gun and Bullets) are so much a part of you, that you treat missing ammunition as if it were a wound that you can restore with Mana. Yeah, it leverages the Arcana less, but it offers &quot;near endless ammo&quot; in a way that doesn't require much stretching.<br /> <br /> For the 5th power, what about allowing you to treat Aiming with the weapon as a Yantra bonus? Spend 3 turns aiming/concentrating, get a +3 Yantra bonus (or less for less turns spent, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-23-2017, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T20:14:06-08:00","id":1170346,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of save or die magic, so not big on the fifth dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T07:48:29-08:00","id":1170425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1165571-homebrew-arcane-archery?p=1170346#post1170346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a fan of save or die magic, so not big on the fifth dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unmaking(/Making) magic already works that way, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Death</b> - Obvious, but technically Making<br /> <b>Fate</b> - Miracle, but again, it's Making<br /> <b>Forces</b> - Eradicate Energy<br /> <b>Life</b> - Life Unmaking kills a target outright (described in Creative Thaum section as an example)<br /> <b>Matter</b> - Doesn't have an effect that will kill you outright already written, but both Making &amp; Unmaking can do the job indirectly with a little effort<br /> <b>Mind</b> - Exceptionally potent Mind Wipe, or a Creative Thaum spell that works as the inverse of Psychic Genesis<br /> <b>Prime</b> - Doesn't have an effect that will kill you outright already written, can't really come up with one without investing more time than I am willing to do<br /> <b>Space</b> - Quarantine + Indefinite<br /> <b>Spirit</b> - Annihilate Spirit, but only for Spirits, obviously.<br /> <b>Time</b> - This is actually Time 4, but Indefinite Temporal Stutter. I suppose you could Unmake someone's entire Timeline with Time 5<br /> <br /> The primary difference between the merit and these effects, I think, is that the merit does this for free, while several of the Arcana would require investing in Indefinite Durations and hoping the spell doesn't get dispelled, or at least wading into Creative Thaumaturgy. <br /> <br /> Half of them can still permanently annihilate a subject entirely with Lasting consequences, though, and of the remaining half, only two struggle with a comparable effect (Prime, and Mind if you don't allow an inverse Psychic Genesis).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T21:34:41-08:00","id":1170596,"title":"","content":"Finally, I can make Green Arrow wannabe! \u2764\ufe0f<br /> <br /> General Note - Adamantine Arrow Status is not really needed. After all this centuries of Diamond cooperation, EVERY Order could have Arcane Archer or two. Most will surely be in Arrows as they are natural fit - but I can think about few concepts that come from other Orders. For example, I plan to run Mage chronicle about Nameless War when we will get Tome of Pentacle - I very much want to propose 19th Century Arcane Gunner for player to it, with Colts and all. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}